WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.234
We are learning of

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.269
more missed warning signs for the company

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.571
behind the Titan submersible

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.306
that imploded on a mission

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.374
to the Titanic.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.608
According to The New Yorker,

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.642
David Lockridge,

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.877
who was a former Ocean

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:11.611
Gate employee

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.445
who claims that he was

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.613
wrongfully terminated

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.215
for raising red flags,

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:18.418
one sent an ominous email to a colleague

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.320
about the doomed vessel writing.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.322
That sub is an accident

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.690
waiting to happen.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.225
He also added this about then

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.393
CEO Stockton Rush.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:26.693
He said,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.661
I don't want to be seen as a tattletale,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.996
but I'm worried

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:32.899
He kills himself and others in a quest

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.934
to boost his ego.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.269
Rush, of course, was among five

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.505
people who died in the tragedy.

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:39.873
Joining me now is Ben

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.241
Taub of The New Yorker

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.910
who wrote this really incredible story.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.378
Ben, and you obtained

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.312
this never before

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:46.980
seen report

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.148
by David Lockridge,

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.316
the fired Ocean Gate employee

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.051
And it details

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.185
so many issues

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.453
that he found with the sub

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.821
during an inspection.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.556
Tell us more about what he

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.624
found in this report.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:00.460
Sure.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:00.794
Yeah.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:01.995
David Lockridge

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:02.562
was perhaps

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.130
the only highly experienced

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:04.964
submarine pilot

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.833
who worked at Ocean Gate at the time,

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:07.700
and he was hired

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.969
as the director of Marine Operations.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.504
And as part of that role,

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.339
as they transitioned from the building

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.108
phase into the testing phase,

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.576
he was required to sign off

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.344
that this was safe to dove.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.580
So he was raising concerns on the

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.781
on the factory floor

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.383
for much of the latter

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.051
half of 2017

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.120
and was just constantly being dismissed,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:27.921
at which point

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.456
he decided he was going to take

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.291
this serious inspection report

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.492
and he was going to detail everything

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.293
in writing

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.194
and submit it

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.795
in writing to Stockton Branch,

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.796
the CEO,

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.098
and Tony Nelson,

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.732
the director of engineering.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:40.733
And in this

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.702
over the next sort of day of

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.038
it was January 18th. 2018.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:47.307
So more than five years ago

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.942
Lockridge inspected every piece,

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.577
every major component of the sub

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:50.977
and found

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.112
that glue was coming away

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.013
from the scenes of the ballast bags.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.381
You had mounting bolts

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.883
threatening to rupture things,

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:57.717
sealing faces

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.486
that had errant punch holes

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:00.253
over in grooves

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.722
that deviated from standard parameters.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:03.990
Everything that could go wrong

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:04.958
was sort of going wrong.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.593
There were snagging hazards

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:07.327
that were important

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.229
components attached with zip ties,

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.164
flammable flooring

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.298
and the internal interior

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.500
vinyl wrapping would emit

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.935
highly toxic gases upon ignition.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:18.371
But the number one concern for Lockridge

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:20.173
was that the actual core

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.574
of this submarine,

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.475
the pressure boundary,

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:25.111
which is what keeps people alive at

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.915
3800 meters where Titanic is,

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.116
where the external water

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.185
pressure is, about £6,000 per square

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.120
inch is made of carbon fiber,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.922
which is not used at the in

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.056
deep ocean submersibles

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.491
because under compression

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.993
it's a capricious material.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.161
It's not made to

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.428
to be used under compression.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:42.996
It's fibers.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.063
It's like rope.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.632
It's strong under tension,

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.133
but not under compression.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.201
So he examined

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.335
a section of it

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.971
and found that it was filled with with,

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:55.108
you know, little, little holes he held.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.210
It was laminating these layers

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.211
it was porous.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.379
He held a light behind it

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.280
and found that the light

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.414
was streaming through.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.516
And he refused to sign off on the diet

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.384
and stuck to in.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.251
Rush said that

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.953
because you refused to sign off

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.821
on this man's testing,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.856
you cannot do your job

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.491
as director of operations.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.259
And so he fired them on the spot.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:13.993
Yeah, in a way.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.728
He was doing the job, Ben,

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.698
and he was fired for doing his job.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.532
And you have to wonder

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.433
what would have happened

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.635
if he'd been able to actually do his job.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.937
So you have in this

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:25.505
you also

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.339
you're interested

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:29.209
in instances where Rush, he seems to take

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:32.412
personal offense to criticism, right?

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.647
Because Lockridge knows people

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.149
outside of Ocean Gate

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:38.952
and there's a coed head of a company

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:42.322
that actually has a classed titanium sub.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:43.089
Of course,

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:43.923
this sub,

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.892
the submersible that imploded,

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.126
it was not classed

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.128
and this co-head of this company says

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:52.365
to him, basically warning him

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:54.000
and he lashes out.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.268
Stockton rushed us, saying

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.437
that he's tired of industry players

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.206
who try to use a safety argument

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.642
to stop innovation.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.812
He seemed so confident that he was doing

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:07.847
something new and different

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:10.016
and that he was being stymied by people

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.452
saying it was in the name of safety.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.453
But he seemed convinced

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.287
it wasn't, even though

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:15.722
truly clearly it was

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:18.324
Yeah.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:18.591
At the

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.292
end of the day,

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.295
this tragedy comes down to hubris.

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:24.430
It was a matter of this kind of,

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:25.632
you know, Silicon

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:27.267
Valley disruptor attitude,

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.568
but it wasn't about

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.702
beating the other companies.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.337
It was about trying to beat physics.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.239
And you're not going to win that.

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.440
And they didn't win that.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.843
And it was sort of blindingly obvious

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:39.212
for four years that this sub was not

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.414
being constructed in a manner

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.216
that would work under great pressure.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.817
You can build as a sub

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.619
that's experimental

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.587
but you can't take passengers

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.122
and that's completely illegal.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.690
And so they structured the company

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.425
such that it was falling outside of U.S.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.627
jurisdiction in various ways.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.196
They had all kinds of sort of steps taken

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.831
so that they weren't actually passengers.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:04:59.732
They were categorized

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:00.933
as mission specialists.

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.935
But how can you have a 19 year old kid

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.437
who's terrified of going inside

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:08.007
in specialists?

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.642
It's completely incoherence.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:12.111
And I imagine that this will, you know,

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.179
this will continue

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.280
for a long time in courts

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.416
because you can only call something

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.017
an accident if it's truly an accident.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.118
And if there's five years

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.520
of very explicit warnings

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.421
from engineers

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:23.523
explaining this is how it will implode,

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.225
and you refuse to to

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.627
to take them seriously.

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:28.561
There has to come a point

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.996
where someone takes responsibility

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:30.630
for that.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.198
Dave Lockridge on the hit for his part

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.800
after he was there.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.702
What's the lesson here on classing

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:37.603
because he was so stocked

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:38.705
in Rush resistant

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:41.474
to having his submersible classed.

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:43.109
And yet what is so clear

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.510
in your report

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.647
is how essential that process is

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:50.083
to providing a submersible

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.584
that is safe for

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:52.919
people to go to these depths.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:55.722
Yeah.

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:58.524
300 meters is not actually you know,

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.426
it is an extreme depth, let's be clear.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.928
But it's not unprecedented.

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:02.762
Nothing he was doing

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:03.930
was breaking boundaries

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:04.464
The boundary

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:05.798
breaking part of this operation

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:06.766
was to try to do it

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.267
in a sub that was unclassified

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.969
and was clearly designed

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:12.672
to do what it did, which was to fail.

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.140
Class submarines can go

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.441
have been going to the Titanic

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.310
since the eighties.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.778
And one of the guys in

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.146
my article had been leading tours

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:20.847
of the Titanic

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:21.748
in the mid 2000

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:22.915
using Soviet submarines

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:24.650
that were built in the eighties.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.352
Others in the article,

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:27.687
because I happened to be at sea with them

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.388
some years ago

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:30.890
for a much more sort of serious venture

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:31.758
where they were sending

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:32.658
a manned submersible

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.560
that was classed to the deepest point

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.395
in each ocean.

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:37.096
The deepest point in the Pacific

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:38.531
Ocean is 11,000 meters.

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:40.166
It's triple the depth of Titanic.

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:41.167
And for that sub

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.101
they took the guy

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:43.503
from the classification agency

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.037
to the bottom of the Mariana Trench.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:45.872
He signed

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.640
that it was unlimited depth

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.809
at the 11,000 meters down.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.344
And for that solved,

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:53.346
you know, in a titanium spherical hull

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.380
which evenly distributes

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.014
the pressure,

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:56.015
not a cylinder

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.117
which will get crushed under pressure.

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.720
Titanium is that titanium sphere hull.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.521
The Titanic didn't

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:03.356
even count as a dove for classification

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.657
and insurance reasons.

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:05.725
Every hundred dives

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.126
you have to do inspections,

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:08.094
but the threshold for

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:09.362
them was 4000 meters.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.763
And if it's above 4000,

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:12.031
Titanic's three 800.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:13.166
It's not even a dove

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:15.201
So the notion that stopped

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:16.969
Rush was doing something innovative.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.337
It's a complete lie.

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:19.205
And basically

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:20.807
he had just changed the narrative

00:07:20.807 --> 00:07:22.241
around the point that it became clear

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:23.376
that they would never get it class

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:24.944
because it was going to be a failure.

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:25.845
And the way that they did

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:27.413
that was to sort of

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:29.982
lie to their mission specialists, again,

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:30.783
their passengers

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:31.918
who they'd misclassified

00:07:31.918 --> 00:07:34.153
on purpose for legal reasons,

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.755
that this, you know,

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:36.389
they stopped trying

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:37.223
to say that it was safe.

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:38.825
They started telling them explicitly,

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:40.326
oh, yeah, it's incredibly dangerous.

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:42.261
You might die. You have to sign a waiver.

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:43.429
This is an experimental sub,

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:44.564
which was true.

00:07:44.564 --> 00:07:45.765
But the lie there was that

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:47.700
this is how serious operation is done.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.035
It's not how it's done at all.

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:51.204
And last thing that I just need to make

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:51.804
very clear

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:52.371
is that Dave

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:53.906
Lockridge actually did raise this

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:54.974
with the US government

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:55.975
after he was fired.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:56.843
He was so concerned

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:58.077
about what was going on

00:07:58.077 --> 00:07:59.779
that he shared his report

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:00.346
with OSHA

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:01.714
and occupational

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:03.649
Safety and Health Administration.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:04.717
And that report was then

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:06.185
passed on from oceans to the US

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:06.953
Coast Guard,

00:08:06.953 --> 00:08:07.420
and there's no

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.754
evidence of any follow up from there.

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:10.923
That was in March of 20. 18.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:13.192
Yeah, you make that so clear.

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.394
He tried to raise some flags

00:08:15.394 --> 00:08:16.462
and in the end

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:18.764
he was buried in legal bills,

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.700
as you describe in your report.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.901
Then excellent reporting.

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:23.536
I think it's such an important lesson

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:25.605
for so many people,

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:27.974
not just when it comes to submersibles

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:29.942
